# Synopsis

Apply a patch to files under the working directory using the V4A patch format
(the "apply_patch" format used by OpenAI Codex).

The tool input is the patch text itself, not JSON.

# Format

    *** Begin Patch
    *** Update File: <path>
    @@ <optional anchor line>
     <context line>
    -<removed line>
    +<added line>
    *** Move to: <new path>
    *** Add File: <path>
    +<content line>
    *** Delete File: <path>
    *** End of File
    *** End Patch

- Every hunk line starts with exactly one of: " " (keep), "+" (add),
  "-" (delete). A blank added line is "+"; a blank context line is " ".
- "@@ <line>" starts the next hunk at that line; the anchor line itself is
  not modified. "@@" alone only separates hunks.
- "*** End of File" anchors a hunk to the end of the file.
- Each path may appear in at most one section per patch.
- Update/Delete require an existing file; Add and Move destinations must not
  exist.
- The patch is all-or-nothing at parse time: an unknown line or an unmatched
  hunk means nothing is applied.

# Returns

One line per applied operation: "created: <path>", "updated '<path>'",
"deleted: <path>", "moved '<from>' to '<to>'", or
"failed to <operation> <path>: <reason>". On a parse failure:
"error at line <n>: ...".

# Notes

Prefer this tool for precise edits to existing files; use the shell tool for
generated files, formatting, or bulk replacements.
